      "content": "You should immediately rinse the wound with plenty of running water and mild soap, but avoid pouring anything directly into the deep hole. Because rusty objects can introduce iron bacteria and you have no access to a doctor today, it is unwise to try sealing a deep, puncture wound without first ruling out the need for professional tetanus care. If it is not directly sealed, cover the area loosely with a clean, sterile bandage to prevent further contamination while you finish your project. Please prioritize your health and be aware that infection risks from deep puncture wounds still require medical attention even if you can avoid it.",
